A script (top-level statements, no :CLASS) that reaches for Base:. Outside
a class there is no parent to delegate to, so the reference is an error
(diag.base_outside_class, error tier: any top-level statement makes the
file a script, issue #255). The member access on another receiver
(oUri:Base) is a near miss that must stay silent (diag.base_standalone
D10 exemption).
-- input.ssl --
:PARAMETERS oUri;
:DECLARE sRoot, nCount;
nCount := 1;
sRoot := oUri:Base;
Base:Init();
:RETURN sRoot;
-- format --
:PARAMETERS oUri;
:DECLARE sRoot, nCount;

nCount := 1;
sRoot := oUri:Base;
Base:Init();

:RETURN sRoot;
-- diagnostics --
5:1-5:5 error base_outside_class: 'Base:MemberName' can only be used inside a ':CLASS' definition
-- diagnostics [--strict --info] --
5:1-5:5 error base_outside_class: 'Base:MemberName' can only be used inside a ':CLASS' definition
